WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.934
-Thank you and welcome, welcome,

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.903
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.104
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, you're here.

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.773
[ Whistling ]
Thank you very much.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.675
Well, guys, as much
as we'd like to move on,

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:12.078
former President Trump
is still in the news.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.413
We thought we drove him
to a farm upstate,

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:17.250
but he somehow found his way
back home to the headlines.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.617
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.786
Yeah, last night,
House impeachment managers

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.189
delivered the impeachment
article against Trump

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.390
to the Senate.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.626
If you missed it,
here they are walking it over.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:35.735 line:0%
[ Camera shutters
clicking continuously ]

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.871 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.709 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.577 line:0%
Okay, alright, okay, yeah, okay.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.745
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:48.147
After 45 minutes,
they were like,

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.415
"Wait, does anyone know
where we're going?"

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.751
It's like, "No.
I'm following you.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.520
I thought you --"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.956
Yeah, it turns out half of them
were delivering the articles.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.791
The other half were just
getting in their steps.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.092
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.227
I say forget impeachment.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.495
Just having Trump make that walk

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.696
would be punishment enough.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.897
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.866
It looked like a wedding,
when the deejay says,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.935
"Table 6,
you can go to the salad bar."

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.570
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.738
Yeah, the walk was pretty long
and drawn out.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.640
It kind of reminded me
of something, though.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.477
[ George Baker Selection's
"Little Green Bag" plays ]

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:27.319 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:28.555 line:0%
♪ Yeah ♪

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:31.123 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.425 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:35.194 line:0%
-♪ Lookin' for some happiness ♪

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.630 line:0%
♪ But there is only loneliness ♪

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.697 line:0%
♪ To find ♪

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.132 line:0%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.167 line:0%
[ Whistling ]

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.502
-I knew it.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.370
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.172
Well, speaking
of the former president,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.708
sources in touch with Trump
have said he's...

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.711
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.245
Well, he was already
out of his mind,

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.480
so I guess, now,
he's just bored.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.082
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.784
Apparently, playing 36 holes
of golf every day

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:01.621
isn't as exciting when you're
not ignoring a global pandemic.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.089
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.291
But today, Trump's aides
were trying to cheer him up.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.526
They were like,
"Good news, sir.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.094
Your trial starts in two weeks."

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.962
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.830
Meanwhile,
President Biden's very busy

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.966 line:0%
and, today, he spoke
with Vladimir Putin

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.535 line:0%
for the first time
since taking office.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.571
As soon as the call began,
Trump was like --

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.707
[ As Trump ]
I feel a disturbance
in the force.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.342
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.744
But this is good --
Biden actually pressed Putin

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.480
on last year's massive
Russian cyber attack.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.848
Putin denied it, but it got
weird when he was like --

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:31.951
[ As Putin ]
By the way, nice purple tie.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.753
He's like, "Wait.
We're not on Zoom.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.887
How did you know that was...?"

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.322
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.557
I think you can tell Putin
was used to talking to Trump

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.460
because, out of habit,
he ended the call with --

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.594
[ As Putin ]
Love you, too.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.563
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:47.467
[ Applause ]

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.602
Some tech news --
I saw that Apple has issued

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.204 line:0%
a new warning to customers.
Listen to this.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:55.241 line:0%
-An important health warning
for all iPhone users.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.511 line:0%
Apple warns customers that
the smartphones could interfere

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:03.616 line:0%
with medical devices,
most notably, pacemakers.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.518
This is bad news
for all the grandmothers

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.453
who like to connect
their iPhone to a chest mount

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.589
when they do base jumping.
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.890
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.092
It'll be weird when a guy
is like, "I love this phone.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.028
Hey, Siri,
turn off my pacemaker."

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.729
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.729 --> 00:03:20.199
And get this -- I saw
that Tyson Foods is releasing

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:24.103 line:0%
heart-shaped chicken nuggets
for Valentine's Day.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.105 line:0%
Or, as I always say,
if you want to keep it classy,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.474 line:0%
go with the standard scratch-off
ticket and beef jerky.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:32.578
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.146
Seriously, that makes
an edible arrangement

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:35.548
look like a diamond necklace.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.782
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:38.651
Yeah, you can sprinkle
the nuggets on your bed

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:41.386
and then uncover her eyes
and watch her as she says,

00:03:41.386 --> 00:03:42.554
"I'm going to stay
at my sister's."

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:45.157
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.460
But they're on your side
of the bed, honey!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.295
[ Applause ]

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.597
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.232
I could hold you up by your legs

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.034
and you could just eat them off
like a --

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.102
[ Laughter ]
like a nugget stand,

00:03:57.102 --> 00:03:59.138
like a keg stand, but like a --

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.239
Like an anteater.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.442
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.244
Look, I won't judge, but if your
Valentine's Day plan involves

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.546
the words dipping sauces,

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.914
you might want
to rethink things.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:08.981
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:11.016
Speaking of food,
Panera has created

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:14.887 line:0%
