00:08:38.917 --> 00:08:40.786
-It's a 4x4, yeah.
-Wow.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:41.887
-I mean --
-That's impressive.

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:43.722
I don't know. 4x4? Sure.

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:46.091
[ Laughter ]
Four wheels.

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:48.927
4x4 -- like yeah.
-It's a hell of a jump.

00:08:48.927 --> 00:08:50.663
You have an incredible
vertical, if you do that.

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:53.031
-It's a cube.
It's 4 foot by 4 feet truck.

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:54.533
-Oh.

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.402
-Oh, no.
I jump from the second floor.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.769
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.769 --> 00:09:00.339
I jump out the bedroom window
and land in my truck.

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.874
And then, it's already gotten
onto a song

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.009
and I cruised out,
went to the hardware store

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:06.245
to get a light switch,
like this, like a lamp switch.

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:08.347
-Hm.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:09.581
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:09:09.581 --> 00:09:10.716
That wasn't a "Hm."

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.850
That wasn't an interesting "Hm."

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.519
That was a "Hm" of doubt.
-Yeah.

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:15.488
It was a "Hm" of doubt.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:16.822
-Yeah.
No, I know what this is.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:19.391
To put those clicker
light switches on this,

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.327
you only cut one of the wires,
not both of them.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:23.763
You leave the other one
connected

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:27.433
and then, what it does is it
connects the, you know, the --

00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.368
negative charge.
You want to keep.

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.003
[ Laughter ]
-Got it. Got it.

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:32.437
-You want to keep the positive.
-Really?

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:33.605
-You want to keep that positive

00:09:33.605 --> 00:09:34.774
charge going, yeah.
-Want to accentuate

00:09:34.774 --> 00:09:35.841
the positive.
-Make sure you unplug before you

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:37.243
even mess around
with this stuff, kids.

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.679
-Nice.
-Nothing metal in your hands
or anything.

00:09:39.679 --> 00:09:41.680
-What's that?
-No electricity, no metal

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.681
in your hands.
-No. Don't.

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:43.683
Stay away from water,

00:09:43.683 --> 00:09:44.850
any liquid, stuff like that.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.353
Just your basic
electricity knowledge.

00:09:48.353 --> 00:09:50.722
[ Laughter ]
And so I did that.

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:52.892
I was working. I was ready
to work on that like a project

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:54.893
and then my mind was blown.

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:58.664
I heard the song,
"Swingin'," by Thad Cockrell.

00:09:58.664 --> 00:09:59.965
I go, "I never heard
Thad Cockrell,"

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:01.166
and then I looked him up.

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:04.770
I guess he's been around, so.
But, anyways,

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.972
I was feeling that spirit
of like,

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:08.607
because we were doing
the show from home,

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:10.642
which is just like,

00:10:10.642 --> 00:10:12.144
everybody's trying
to get through the day

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:14.279
and it was like, "We just got
to put on the best thing

00:10:14.279 --> 00:10:16.248
we can possibly do
with what we got, you know?

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:19.051
Don't give up.
Let's keep pushing. Let's go."

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:21.787
And I was feeling that spirit
and then I heard that song.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:23.155
It spoke to me.
I loved it.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:25.624
I asked our booker,
"Can we book him?"

00:10:25.624 --> 00:10:29.194
And tonight he's on the show,
playing with The Roots tonight,

00:10:29.194 --> 00:10:30.296
which is very exciting.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:32.264
[ Cheering and applause ]
It's exciting.

